PROBLEM STATEMENT
Finding convenient and reliable parking is a major challenge in India's crowded urban areas
Drivers waste time searching for parking near malls,stadiums, hospitals, railway stations, and event venues
Uncertain parking availability leads to traffic congestion, fuel wastage, and frustration
Poor parking management, illegal parking, and unclear charges further worsen the problem
In Bengaluru, 28.59 lakh parking violations were recorded between January 2022 and June 2024
Conventional smart parking systems may require costly cameras, boom barriers, and infrastructure modifications
Physical slot markings and hardware costs can make implementation difficult for smaller operators.
There is a need for an economically feasible, scalable, and software-first parking solution
Marga uses AI-assisted virtual slot generation, digital reservations, and automated billing
It aims to organise existing parking spaces while minimising hardware dependency and physical modifications.
PROPOSED SOLUTION 
Marga:
### Marga – AI-Powered Smart Parking Discovery and Management Platform

Marga is an AI-powered, software-first smart parking platform designed to connect drivers, parking facility owners, and mobility service providers through a unified digital ecosystem.

**Working Mechanism:** Parking facility owners register their facilities on Marga's SaaS-based platform, providing site dimensions, boundaries, entrances, obstacles, and vehicle
 requirements. Marga uses AI-assisted layout generation and geometric calculations to create a digital parking map with uniquely numbered virtual slots, even for suitable grounds
  without individually marked spaces. Owners can review and approve the layouts, manage slot availability, configure tariffs, and monitor reservations through a dedicated dashboard.

Users enter their destination or use their current location to discover nearby parking within a configurable radius. Marga displays available facilities, reported slot availability, 
prices, and vehicle compatibility. Its intelligent recommendation engine suggests suitable parking options and alternatives when preferred facilities are full. Users select and reserve
 individual virtual slots, register their vehicle details, and receive a unique booking ID and QR code.

During parking, users or authorised operators confirm check-in and check-out. Marga records parking sessions, calculates duration, applies configured pricing rules, generates digital bills,
 and updates slot availability according to verified parking status. Database transactions prevent overlapping reservations, while separate reservation and occupancy records improve management accuracy.

**SaaS Model and Mobility Integration:** Marga can operate as a Software-as-a-Service platform, allowing multiple parking operators to manage their facilities through a centralised system, 
potentially using subscription-based plans. Future integrations with Uber, Rapido, and other mobility platforms could allow users and drivers to discover nearby parking during journey planning, 
subject to API availability and partnerships.

By combining AI-assisted virtual slot generation, digital reservations, automated billing, operator management, and potential mobility integrations, Marga aims to build a scalable smart
 parking ecosystem without requiring dedicated hardware at every facility.



